cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this project, please cite it as below."
title: "Signal or Noise? A Forward Test and Statistical Post-Mortem of a Multi-Factor Stock Model"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-01
abstract: >-
  A multi-factor US equity model returned +99% (QQQ +37%) in a walk-forward backtest
  (March 2025 to April 2026). With its rules frozen, a $1,000 real-time paper portfolio
  returned -24.3% from 2026-07-09 to the 2026-09-25 close while QQQ returned +3.0%.
  A reproducible statistical post-mortem (block bootstrap, rank information
  coefficients, Brier skill and reliability, multiple-testing, pseudo-replication and
  power analysis) finds no evidence of skill and an implementation mismatch between
  the backtested and the live strategy.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: miemielove520
repository-code: "https://github.com/miemielove520/signal-or-noise"
